      {
        "question_text": "Classify each variable as numerical or categorical and give a reason.\n(a) The number of sheep owned by a farmer.\n(b) The time taken to complete a puzzle.\n(c) A student’s favourite video game console.",
        "solution_text": "(a) **Numerical**: the number of sheep is a count.\n(b) **Numerical**: the time is a measurement.\n(c) **Categorical**: the console name identifies a choice."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A player wears jersey $42$ and scores $42$ goals during a season.\nClassify each recorded variable as numerical or categorical and explain the difference.\n(a) Jersey number.\n(b) Number of goals scored.",
        "solution_text": "(a) **Categorical**: $42$ identifies the player’s jersey; it does not record an amount.\n(b) **Numerical**: $42$ is the count of goals scored.\nThe same digits can be a label or a count. Classify what is being recorded."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Classify the data generated by each survey question as numerical or categorical and give a reason.\n(a) How long does it take you to walk to the library?\n(b) Which is your favourite sport?",
        "solution_text": "(a) **Numerical**: the response is a measured time.\n(b) **Categorical**: the response names a sport."
      }
    ],
